meta {
  name: Add Item
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/cart/items
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "product_id": "{{PRODUCT_ID}}",
    "quantity": 1
  }
}

docs {
  # POST /api/v1/cart/items

  Add a published, in-stock product. No login required.

  The first anonymous add returns `cart_token`. Copy it into the `CART_TOKEN` environment variable and send it as `X-Cart-Token` on later requests. Do not send a price.

  To add as a logged-in shopper, set auth to Bearer `{{ACCESS_TOKEN}}`.

  For a product that has variants (`has_variants` is true in the product detail), send `variant_id` too: the cart line is per variant and its price, SKU and stock come from that variant on the server. A plain product refuses `variant_id`; a variant product refuses a missing one (422). `GET` product detail lists the sellable variants in `variants`.

  `quantity` is 1 to 5, and between the product's `min_per_order` and `max_per_order`. Adding the same product again increases the line, up to 5 and up to the product's stock. Stock is not reduced until an order exists.
}
